    <statement><p>Evaluate the integral:</p>
<p><me>\int_{0}^{t} (5 s {\bf i} + 6 s^2 {\bf j} + 16 {\bf k}) \,ds</me> 
Answer :  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>{\bf i} \, +</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>{\bf j} \, +</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/><m>{\bf k}</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2.5t^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2t^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>16t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int_{0}^{t} 5 s \,ds = \left.\frac{5}{2} s^{2}\right|_{0}^{t}=
 \frac{5}{2} t^2</me>
<me>\int_{0}^{t} 6 s^2 \,ds = \left.\frac{6}{3} s^{3}\right|_0^t=
 2 t^3</me>
<me>\left.\int_{0}^{t} 16 \,ds = 16 s\right|_0^t=16 t</me>
Hence,



<me>\int_{0}^{t} (5 s \bf{i}\it + 6 s^2 \bf{j}\it + 16 \bf{k}\it) \,ds = \left(\int_{0}^{t} 5 s \,ds\right) \bf{i}\it + \left(\int_{0}^{t} 6 s^2 \,ds\right) \bf{j}\it + \left(\int_{0}^{t} 16 \,ds\right) \bf{k}\it</me>


 
<me>=\left(\frac{5}{2} t^2\right)\bf{i}\it + \left(2 t^3\right) \bf{j}\it + \left(16 t\right) \bf{k}\it</me> 



</solution>
